<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<task id="013" project="spaarkeai-assistant-enhancements-r4">
  <metadata>
    <title>E1 eval cases — golden utterances for the task-agenda capability (FR-10)</title>
    <phase>1 — E1 grounded-recommend tier</phase>
    <gate>startable</gate>
    <status>pending</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>TEST-MODIFYING — adds eval/test coverage; CLAUDE.md §8 TEST-MODIFYING override forces code-review + adr-check unconditionally.</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>sonnet</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Well-specified eval-case authoring against an established harness — literal execution against a closed set of golden utterances + assertions; no architectural judgment.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>Wave1-E1</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>true</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-reason>Adds new eval-case files only — no shared-spine edits; runs alongside other Wave1-E1 tasks once 012 lands the capability.</parallel-reason>
    <deps>012</deps>
    <tags>testing, eval, ai</tags>
    <estimated-effort>3-4 hours</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>
  <prompt>Add golden-utterance eval cases that cover the P1 task-agenda behavior (per ADR-039 + the FR-10 eval-case obligation) so the suite FAILS if the capability regresses to a thin ack, fabricates data, or fails to cite. Add cases in the eval-harness location established by task 001 for utterances like "what do I need to do today", "what's on my plate", and prioritization phrasing. Assert: a grounded + cited summary, a recommendation, Tasks-opened, and no-fabrication. Wire the cases into the suite.</prompt>
  <role>SPAARKE test/eval author. Follow ADR-038 (integration-heavy testing) + ADR-039 (golden-utterance eval-case obligation). Comfortable authoring golden-utterance eval cases and wiring them into the existing harness.</role>
  <goal>The P1 behavior is covered by golden-utterance eval cases that fail if the task-agenda capability regresses to a thin ack, fabricates, or fails to cite.</goal>
  <context>
    <background>FR-10 — the eval-case guardrail. ADR-039 + the maker-guide obligation require every new/changed AI behavior to land with an eval case. This task covers the FR-01 task-agenda capability authored in task 012 (the advisory upgrade of `list-tasks`): "what do I need to do today" must yield a grounded, cited summary + a recommendation + Tasks-opened, with no thin ack and no fabricated data. Add golden-utterance cases in the eval-harness location established by task 001 (the project's harness-seeding task) and assert the P1 DoD so a regression breaks the suite. Depends on task 012 (the capability must exist to evaluate).</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file>the eval-harness location established by task 001 (the project's harness-seeding task — add the E1 golden-utterance cases here)</file>
      <file>infra/dataverse/actions/list-tasks.action.json (the advisory capability under test, authored by task 012)</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-039-grounded-execution-closed-catalogs.md (the golden-utterance eval-case obligation)</file>
      <file>docs/adr/ADR-038-testing-strategy.md (integration-heavy pyramid; eval-case obligation)</file>
    </relevant-files>
  </context>
  <constraints>
    <constraint source="ADR-039" scope="the eval cases">Assert the grounded + cited + no-fabrication invariants; a case MUST fail if a narrated fact is uncited or fabricated, or if the capability regresses to a thin ack. The suite MUST NOT assume a second decider exists.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-038" scope="the eval cases">Author as golden-utterance eval cases wired into the established suite; follow the integration-heavy testing strategy + the eval-case obligation.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project" scope="harness location">Add the cases in the harness location established by task 001 — MUST NOT stand up a parallel harness (§11 reuse-first).</constraint>
  </constraints>
  <knowledge>
    <files>
      <file>projects/spaarkeai-assistant-enhancements-r4/spec.md</file>
      <file>projects/spaarkeai-assistant-enhancements-r4/CLAUDE.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-039-grounded-execution-closed-catalogs.md</file>
      <file>docs/adr/ADR-038-testing-strategy.md</file>
    </files>
  </knowledge>
  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="1">Locate the eval-harness location established by task 001 and the case shape it expects.</step>
    <step order="2">Add golden-utterance eval cases for "what do I need to do today", "what's on my plate", and a prioritization phrasing.</step>
    <step order="3">Assert per case: a grounded + cited summary, a recommendation, Tasks-opened, and no-fabrication (a narrated fact with no tool-result citation fails).</step>
    <step order="4">Wire the cases into the suite and run it green.</step>
    <step order="5">Confirm a deliberate regression (thin ack / fabrication / missing citation) makes the cases fail (negative check).</step>
    <step order="6">Update TASK-INDEX ✅.</step>
  </steps>
  <escalation>
    <trigger>If task 001's eval harness does not yet exist or its case shape cannot express the grounded/cited/no-fabrication assertions, STOP and escalate rather than standing up a parallel harness.</trigger>
  </escalation>
  <justification>
    <existing>Task 001 establishes the project's eval harness; the FR-01 capability (task 012) is the behavior under test.</existing>
    <extension>Add E1 golden-utterance cases to the existing harness — no new harness.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>The P1 task-agenda behavior can silently regress to a thin ack / fabrication with no failing test (FR-10 obligation unmet).</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>
  <outputs>
    <output type="test">E1 golden-utterance eval cases in the task-001 harness location (task-agenda capability)</output>
  </outputs>
  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">Eval cases for "what do I need to do today" / "what's on my plate" / prioritization phrasing are added and pass green.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Each case asserts a grounded + cited summary, a recommendation, and Tasks-opened.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">A regression (thin ack / fabrication / missing citation) makes the cases fail (negative case).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The cases are wired into the established eval suite.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>
  <notes>Depends on task 012 (the advisory capability must exist to evaluate) and task 001 (the eval harness). This is the FR-10 guardrail for the P1 DoD.</notes>
  <execution>
    <skill>.claude/skills/task-execute/SKILL.md</skill>
    <protocol>Before starting, load all files in knowledge/files. Follow task-execute skill.</protocol>
  </execution>
</task>
